@startuml 03a-patron-por-modulo
' Estructura interna de un módulo de src/TurisClick.Api/Modules y cómo la cumple cada módulo.
' Evidencia: Modules/*/*ModuleExtensions.cs (registro DI) y los constructores de cada Service/Repository.
!pragma layout smetana
!include ../_tema.iuml
hide empty members
hide circle
skinparam nodesep 35
skinparam ranksep 40

title Backend — patrón interno de un módulo (ejemplo real: Auth) y su grado de cumplimiento

package "Modules/Auth" {
  class AuthController <<Controllers>> #E3F2FD
  class "AuthService" as AuthService <<Services · IAuthService>> #E8F5E9
  class "JwtTokenService" as JwtTokenService <<Services · ITokenService>> #E8F5E9
  class "UserRepository" as UserRepository <<Repositories · IUserRepository>> #FFF8E1
  class "RefreshTokenRepository" as RefreshTokenRepository <<Repositories · IRefreshTokenRepository>> #FFF8E1
  class "User, RefreshToken" as Entities <<Entities>> #F5F5F5
  class "LoginRequest, AuthResultResponse, ..." as Dtos <<Dtos>> #F5F5F5
  class "UserConfiguration,\nRefreshTokenConfiguration" as Config <<Persistence · IEntityTypeConfiguration>> #F5F5F5
  class "AuthModuleExtensions\n.AddAuthModule()" as Ext <<registro DI>> #F5F5F5
}

package "Infrastructure" {
  class TurisClickDbContext <<Database · Scoped = Unit of Work>> #E1F5FE
  class "PasswordHasherService" as Hasher <<Security · IPasswordHasherService>> #E1F5FE
  class "CurrentUserContext" as Cuc <<Security · ICurrentUserContext>> #E1F5FE
}

AuthController --> AuthService : un método\npor acción
AuthController ..> Dtos
AuthService --> UserRepository
AuthService --> RefreshTokenRepository
AuthService --> JwtTokenService
AuthService --> Hasher
AuthService --> Cuc
AuthService --> TurisClickDbContext : SaveChanges /\ntransacción
UserRepository --> TurisClickDbContext : consultas LINQ
RefreshTokenRepository --> TurisClickDbContext
UserRepository ..> Entities
TurisClickDbContext ..> Config : ApplyConfigurationsFromAssembly
Ext ..> AuthService : AddScoped

legend bottom left
<b>Cumplimiento real por módulo</b> (constructores de cada clase)
|= Módulo |= Repositorios propios |= Services que además consultan DbSets directamente (db.X) |
| Auth | User, RefreshToken | AuthService (RefreshTokens) |
| Companies | Company | — |
| Destinations | Destination | PublicDestinationService (Experiences, Packages) |
| Categories | Category | — |
| Experiences | Experience, ExperienceAvailability | ExperienceService (Images), ExperienceAvailabilityService |
| Packages | Package, PackageAvailability | PackageService (Images, Items), PackageAvailabilityService |
| Reservations | Reservation, ReservationItem | ReservationService, ReservationBookingService (UPDATE condicional de cupo), ReservationExpirationService, ReservationCancellationService, PaymentLedger, AdminPaymentsService |
| Ai | AiConversation, AiItinerary, AiCatalog | AiConversationService (db.Set) |
| Flights | <color:#B71C1C>ninguno</color> | PackageFlightService, FlightBookingOrchestrator, FlightReconciliationService |
| Preferences | <color:#B71C1C>ninguno</color> | TouristPreferenceService |
| Admin | <color:#B71C1C>ninguno</color> | AdminUserService, AdminContentService, AdminOnboardingService, AdminPlatformService |

Todos los Services reciben <b>TurisClickDbContext</b> (Unit of Work: SaveChanges, BeginTransaction,
ExecuteUpdate condicional). La regla documentada "el Service nunca consulta el DbContext" se cumple
sólo en Companies y Categories. No existe capa Domain/Application separada ni repositorio genérico.
endlegend

@enduml
